{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1552560-aren-t-balance-and-burden-too-harsh","id":1552560,"title":"Aren't Balance and Burden too harsh?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-21T08:54:25-07:00","id":1552560,"title":"Aren't Balance and Burden too harsh?","content":"I'm reading MtC 2nd Ed right now, and I'm under the impression that their Anchors are the hardest to use from the whole Chronicles. Is there something I didn't understood, or is it intentional? Are there better rules for them in supplements?<br /> <br /> Even recovering a single Willpower Point seems to require a meaningful decision that can't be taken lightly by the player. Full recovery is such a high bar that I can't easily see it happening more than a couple times through a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Arisen can recover from death, but that has a heavy cost on Memory at the very least. And while Burden is easier to apply, it requires a high level of assholery, usually against your meret. Isn't it too dysfunctional?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T10:14:39-07:00","id":1552562,"title":"","content":"The thresholds for Willpower recovery through Balance and Burden are the same approximate degree of narrative weight as other gamelines with Anchors that offer single-point and full-refill recovery. I feel as though Geist's formatting framing the recovery limits for Root and Bloom as once-per-scene and once-per-story respectively is salient, as is Promethean's additional mechanics for the Torment Anchor as &quot;penalize your next roll to resist Torment by -1&quot; and &quot;immediately check for Torment.&quot;<br /> <br /> As with getting Beats for resolving Conditions, consequentiality matters, but the single-point refresh just necessitates facing a relevant challenge or demonstrating a moment of weakness.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting Mummies can regain Willpower from meditation (as an alternative to sleep), which they also do to recover Pillars, and can burn a dot of Sekhem in a pinch to fully refill their Willpower; this isn't a Vampire situation where the Arisen are constantly at risk of hollowing out from their normal operations and/or one rough fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T03:41:37-07:00","id":1552581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1552560-aren-t-balance-and-burden-too-harsh#post1552560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, the Arisen can recover from death, but that has a heavy cost on Memory at the very least.?</div> </div> </div> </div>About this, i could be wrong but i remember that in 1ed you lose 1 memory dot after a resurrection, right?<br /> <br /> But in 2ed i don t see that loss.<br /> Have i missed it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T05:04:43-07:00","id":1552584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1552560-aren-t-balance-and-burden-too-harsh?p=1552581#post1552581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About this, i could be wrong but i remember that in 1ed you lose 1 memory dot after a resurrection, right?<br /> <br /> But in 2ed i don t see that loss.<br /> Have i missed it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember the page right now, but you roll a dice pool upon resurrection, and sets Memory by successes, capped at 3.<br /> <br /> Now, it could be that this is only at a brand new Descent, it's hard to say. A previous excerpt seems to contradict this, and overall I found the Core Mummy book quite badly written and hard to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T07:28:47-07:00","id":1552586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1552560-aren-t-balance-and-burden-too-harsh?p=1552581#post1552581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About this, i could be wrong but i remember that in 1ed you lose 1 memory dot after a resurrection, right?<br /> <br /> But in 2ed i don t see that loss.<br /> Have i missed it?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1552560-aren-t-balance-and-burden-too-harsh?p=1552584#post1552584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember the page right now, but you roll a dice pool upon resurrection, and sets Memory by successes, capped at 3.<br /> <br /> Now, it could be that this is only at a brand new Descent, it's hard to say. A previous excerpt seems to contradict this, and overall I found the Core Mummy book quite badly written and hard to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mummy starts each Descent at Memory 0 and resets to their listed Memory score after that first scene. Neither edition has losing Memory as a standard consequence of normal death, though 1e has falling to Duat lower a mummy's Memory by 1 to a minimum of 3 and 2e has the Trials of Duat end with Anpu offering an optional drink to guarantee an extra starting dot of Sekhem on the next arising in exchange for a one-die breaking point.<br /> <br /> The consequences of normal death and resurrection from the subsequent death cycle are purely Sekhem-related; in both editions, you make a Memory roll, then make another Memory roll modified by the previous one's result, and the result on the second Memory roll affects how much Sekhem you lose or potentially lose upon returning to life (linearly proceeding from two dots on a dramatic failure to a single Descent roll on an exceptional success).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T18:58:17-07:00","id":1552679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1552560-aren-t-balance-and-burden-too-harsh?p=1552586#post1552586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mummy starts each Descent at Memory 0 and resets to their listed Memory score after that first scene. Neither edition has losing Memory as a standard consequence of normal death, though 1e has falling to Duat lower a mummy's Memory by 1 to a minimum of 3 and 2e has the Trials of Duat end with Anpu offering an optional drink to guarantee an extra starting dot of Sekhem on the next arising in exchange for a one-die breaking point.<br /> <br /> The consequences of normal death and resurrection from the subsequent death cycle are purely Sekhem-related; in both editions, you make a Memory roll, then make another Memory roll modified by the previous one's result, and the result on the second Memory roll affects how much Sekhem you lose or potentially lose upon returning to life (linearly proceeding from two dots on a dramatic failure to a single Descent roll on an exceptional success).</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 165, <b>Death and Resurrection</b>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummies that return to life must roll their highest Pillar rating to complete the Death Cycle. For every success, they earn a dot of Memory with which they awake, to a maximum of 3. </div> </div> </div>Upon re-reading it, it's clear that this is just about resurrection within the same Semektet. Also it's probably just for the first scene, <i><b>but that's not what is actually written</b></i>. As written, it make seems like Resurrecting costs you all your Memory.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you're right, I'm just stating for the sake of explaining where did I get this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}